        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "A further new compound was found in the as-cast samples containing 16.6 at.% Er. The X-ray powder pattern of this compound was very similar to the powder pattern of the ErNi₄B boride. The crystal structure of the new Er₀.₉₁₇Ni₄.₀₉B boride was determined using an X-ray single-crystal method: space group P6/mmm; a = 1.48399 nm; c = 0.69194 nm [15]. This structure is very similar to the Y₀.₉₁₅Ni₄.₁₂B structure [16]. The Er₀.₉₁₇Ni₄.₀₉B boride decomposes after annealing, and the main phase is the ErNi₄B compound.",
